{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1130450-broad-question-any-way-to-know-how-a-freelancer-submission-went","id":1130450,"title":"Broad question: any way to know how a freelancer submission went?","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Additional Discussion","Off-Topic"],"posts":[{"date":"2017-08-17T13:45:58-07:00","id":1130450,"title":"Broad question: any way to know how a freelancer submission went?","content":"Because I read the brochure and the &quot;damn, I'd really like to write some of these books myself&quot; thought returned at full strength<br /> <br /> A few months ago I sent in my first freelancer submission and, while I'm not saying that should have got me a job at Onyx Path for sure, I have no idea how that went. I'm not even sure if it was considered or not. I <i>do </i>think to have followed all the technical guidelines: the length, the division between crunch and fluff, a signed disclosure form and all the attachments, but I can't be 100% sure I did no mistakes.<br /> <br /> Since enough time has passed for me to send in another, I'd really like to know how the first one went, whether it was a &quot;sorry, you're not what we're looking for right now&quot; or a &quot;sorry but you messed up the guidelines so the submission was not valid in the first place&quot;. I would not mind rejection nor being told I made errors, but that would be useful to know in order the prepare future ones better and try again. I don't want to make the same mistakes over and over.<br /> <br /> Writing to the developers directly does sound rude and unprofessional, all things considered, so I'm asking to anyone that's willing to reply: is there a way to know what happened to my first submission?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T13:47:56-07:00","id":1130452,"title":"","content":"I don't think this company notifies the folks they turn down. Odds are if you haven't heard back for a couple of months, you probably got shot down.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Remi. she/her. game designer.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/281-atamajakki","name":"atamajakki","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar281_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5487"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-08-17T14:25:41-07:00","id":1130481,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>atamajakki</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/general/off-topic/1130450-broad-question-any-way-to-know-how-a-freelancer-submission-went?p=1130452#post1130452\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I don't think this company notifies the folks they turn down. Odds are if you haven't heard back for a couple of months, you probably got shot down.</div> </div> </div> </div>My guess as well, but I admit knowing that was the case and that I got the submission guidelines right would be useful. In theory, the submission guide says the company tries to respond all the entries, which is the reason I'm asking<br /> <br /> (It probably just got shot down though)","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/815620-cinder-s-comprehensive-collection-of-creations\" target=\"_blank\">Cinder's Comprehensive Collection of Creations</a> - Homebrew Hub<br /> <br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/beast-the-primordial-aa/1172470-cinder-writes-about-beast-the-primordial\" target=\"_blank\">I write about Beast: The Primordial a lot</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/38-cinder","name":"Cinder","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar38_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1408"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}